MustardOS for R36S/R35S (unofficial port)
Copyright (c) 2026 MustardOS R36S/R35S port contributors

This is an unofficial port of MustardOS (also known as muOS) to the
RK3326 R36S/R35S handhelds. It is not made, approved, endorsed or
supported by the MustardOS project. "MustardOS" and "muOS" are the names
of the MustardOS project and are used here only to say what this port is
based on (https://muos.dev/press, https://muos.dev/docs/tou). Support:
https://github.com/laurorual/MustardOS-R36S-port/issues

The port's own code is under the MIT licence (LICENSE). Patches to, and
files derived from, third-party code (for example configuration files
adapted from MustardOS) are under that code's licence (GPL-2.0,
GPL-3.0, ...).

The firmware image combines many third-party components, each under its
own licence: the MustardOS frontend and scripts (GPL-3.0), MustardOS
themes and assets (CC BY-NC 4.0), the Linux kernel and U-Boot (GPL-2.0),
Buildroot packages, libretro cores and standalone emulators (GPL, Zlib,
BSD and non-commercial licences), Rockchip boot payloads (rkbin licence)
and closed components (the Arm Mali userspace driver, DraStic). The full
list with versions, licences and states is in docs/LICENSING.md and in
/usr/share/muos-r35s/THIRD-PARTY.txt inside the image. The corresponding
source of every release is published with the release.

Non-commercial licences apply to some cores: the firmware must not be
sold or bundled with a commercial product.

No games, BIOS files or other copyrighted content are included.
